    "rr": 1.0
   },
   "answer": "BERT masks 15% of all WordPiece tokens in each sequence at random [c_1]. Each chosen token is replaced as follows:\n\n- **80% of the time:** it becomes the [MASK] token [c_1].\n- **10% of the time:** it becomes a random token [c_1].\n- **10% of the time:** it stays unchanged [c_1].\n\nThe model then uses the final hidden vector Ti to predict the original token, trained with cross-entropy loss [c_1].\n\nThe mixed strategy is meant to reduce the mismatch between pre-training and fine-tuning, because the [MASK] token never appears during fine-tuning [c_1][c_3]. Keeping the word unchanged biases the representation toward the actual observed word [c_2]. Random replacement affects only 1.5% of all tokens (10% of 15%), which does not seem to harm language understanding [c_2].",
   "citations": [
