   "answer": "The experiment showed that RAG's accuracy drops sharply when the index doesn't match the time period of the question. The authors built a 2016 index (the DrQA Wikipedia dump from December 2016) and compared it with the newer December 2018 index. They then queried an NQ RAG model with \"Who is {position}?\" for 82 world leaders who had changed between those dates [c_1].\n\n- **Matched indices:** RAG answered 70% correctly using the 2016 index for 2016 leaders, and 68% using the 2018 index for 2018 leaders [c_1].\n- **Mismatched indices:** Accuracy was low, at 12% with the 2018 index and 2016 leaders, and 4% with the 2016 index and 2018 leaders [c_1].\n\nThe authors conclude that RAG's world knowledge can be updated simply by replacing its non-parametric memory [c_1].",
